WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:05.560
A mouse cannot say a touch feels nice.

2
00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:09.060
Which of its cells detect a stroke, and what can we measure?

3
00:00:10.133 --> 00:00:14.873
In mouse hairy skin, at least three afferent classes are candidates for detecting a

4
00:00:14.873 --> 00:00:15.873
stroke.

5
00:00:16.133 --> 00:00:20.693
First, unmyelinated touch afferents marked by tyrosine hydroxylase.

6
00:00:21.513 --> 00:00:24.093
Their endings run lengthwise along a hair follicle.

7
00:00:25.117 --> 00:00:30.897
Second, unmyelinated neurons marked by a receptor called MrgprB4.

8
00:00:31.697 --> 00:00:33.657
Their fibres innervate hairy skin only.

9
00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:37.360
Third, Aβ beta field afferents.

10
00:00:37.360 --> 00:00:40.680
They are myelinated, and their endings wrap around the follicle.

11
00:00:41.650 --> 00:00:44.090
A field afferent ignores any single hair.

12
00:00:44.990 --> 00:00:47.250
Indenting the skin drives it only at high force.

13
00:00:49.733 --> 00:00:54.773
But one neuron can form as many as 180 endings, around many follicles.

14
00:00:55.817 --> 00:01:00.357
Predict. What does a gentle stroke across the skin do to this neuron?

15
00:01:06.467 --> 00:01:11.767
It fires. The authors proposed that it sums many weakly sensitive endings.

16
00:01:12.867 --> 00:01:14.367
A single hair is a lever.

17
00:01:15.247 --> 00:01:16.587
A field afferent is a net.

18
00:01:20.067 --> 00:01:26.727
Now the outcomes. Activating MrgprB4 neurons gave young male mice a place

19
00:01:26.727 --> 00:01:27.727
preference.

20
00:01:29.217 --> 00:01:33.757
The authors read this as positive reinforcement, reduced anxiety, or both.

21
00:01:34.750 --> 00:01:39.830
Adult females whose lineage of these cells was removed during development were less

22
00:01:39.830 --> 00:01:40.850
sexually receptive.

23
00:01:42.983 --> 00:01:48.243
A permanent genetic label marks neurons that once expressed the gene, including some

24
00:01:48.243 --> 00:01:49.763
that no longer do in adults.

25
00:01:50.933 --> 00:01:55.833
And a dopamine-sensor signal in the nucleus accumbens was reduced during mounting.

26
00:01:57.733 --> 00:02:01.333
A chamber preference, a mating behaviour, a dopamine signal.

27
00:02:02.253 --> 00:02:03.833
Each is an outcome, not a feeling.

28
00:02:04.883 --> 00:02:06.163
Back to the one idea.

29
00:02:07.043 --> 00:02:10.743
In people, one fibre has a caress-shaped curve that pleasantness follows.

30
00:02:13.433 --> 00:02:17.693
Which mouse cell, if any, matches that human fibre is still unsettled.

31
00:02:18.567 --> 00:02:22.887
Keep the human candidate and the mouse outcomes apart until a match is made.
